00:09:06,085 --> 00:09:08,165
Je sais pas. Est-ce que quelqu'un qui approche la trentaine
I don't know. Would somebody close to 30

171
00:09:08,245 --> 00:09:09,645
et qui n'a jamais joué
who's never acted before

172
00:09:09,725 --> 00:09:12,245
mais qui a eu un petit rôle dans le film de Valérie Donzelli
but had a small part
in Valérie Donzelli's movie

173
00:09:12,325 --> 00:09:13,725
t'intéresserait ?
be of any interest to you?

174
00:09:13,805 --> 00:09:15,605
Bien sûr que je te signerais dans mon agence.
Of course I'd sign you with my agency.

175
00:09:16,885 --> 00:09:18,325
Alors tu as pris ta décision ?
So you've made up your mind?

176
00:09:18,405 --> 00:09:19,805
Tu vas devenir acteur ?
You're going to be an actor?

177
00:09:20,765 --> 00:09:22,405
Je sais pas, c'est trop risqué.
I don't know, it's too risky.

178
00:09:25,325 --> 00:09:27,765
De toute façon, il y aura toujours un bureau pour toi dans mon agence.
Either way, there'll always be a desk
for you at my agency.

179
00:09:28,445 --> 00:09:30,405
Ouais, mais j'en ai marre des bureaux.
Yeah, but I've had it with desks.

180
00:09:32,045 --> 00:09:33,365
On en reparlera plus tard.
We'll talk about it later.

181
00:09:42,325 --> 00:09:43,205
Comment tu te sens ?
How do you feel?

182
00:09:44,845 --> 00:09:46,885
C'est plutôt moi qui devrais te poser la question.
Shouldn't I be asking you?

183
00:09:47,885 --> 00:09:49,565
Je n'ai pas eu de crise cardiaque.
I didn't have a heart attack.

184
00:09:59,645 --> 00:10:01,845
Tu vas vraiment me laisser produire le film de Beauvois ?
Are you really going to let me produce
Beauvois's movie?

185
00:10:02,845 --> 00:10:04,925
J'y pense depuis l'hôpital.
I've been thinking about it
since the hospital.

186
00:10:05,925 --> 00:10:07,845
J'aurais préféré te le dire en tête-à-tête...
I'd rather have told you one-on-one...

187
00:10:09,565 --> 00:10:12,205
Mathias, ce n'est pas une stratégie, j'espère ?
Mathias, this isn't a strategy, is it?

188
00:10:12,965 --> 00:10:15,165
Ce n'est pas du tout une stratégie, Noémie.
It's not a strategy at all, Noémie.

189
00:10:16,205 --> 00:10:18,925
Je te laisse produire le film parce que tu en es capable.
I'm letting you produce the film
because you can do it.

190
00:10:19,005 --> 00:10:20,965
Tu as tout ce qu'il faut pour être une grande productrice.
You have all the makings
of a great producer.

191
00:10:22,645 --> 00:10:25,885
Et le stress d'un producteur... c'est plus pour moi.
Plus, a producer's stress is...
It's no longer for me.

192
00:10:30,165 --> 00:10:31,525
Je ne sais pas quoi dire.
I don't know what to say.

193
00:10:33,845 --> 00:10:37,165
C'est un beau cadeau que tu me fais.
It's a beautiful gift you've given me.

194
00:10:37,245 --> 00:10:38,885
Tu vas faire un grand film.
You're going to make a great film.

195
00:10:39,605 --> 00:10:40,485
Je l'espère.
I hope so.

196
00:10:43,725 --> 00:10:46,805
Mon vrai cadeau, c'est... que tu prennes soin de toi.
My real gift is...
you taking good care of yourself.

197
00:10:47,445 --> 00:10:49,725
-On passe à la distribution ? -Oui...
-Want to go through the cast?
-Yes...

198
00:11:16,285 --> 00:11:17,765
Sayonara.
Sayonara.

199
00:11:27,005 --> 00:11:27,885
Un pastis !
A pastis!

200
00:11:28,725 --> 00:11:31,005
Mais Jean, il est 10h du matin...
Oh, but Jean, it's 10 am...

201
00:11:31,085 --> 00:11:32,605
Et on doit parler.
And we have to talk.

202
00:11:32,685 --> 00:11:34,565
Alors il faut qu'on soit à égalité.
So we have to be on equal footing.

203
00:11:35,645 --> 00:11:36,845
T'en es à combien ?
How many have you had?

204
00:11:36,925 --> 00:11:37,885
C'est le deuxième.
This is my second.

205
00:11:40,525 --> 00:11:41,725
Ça ne te ressemble pas.
It's not like you.

206
00:11:41,805 --> 00:11:43,045
Voilà.
There.

207
00:11:43,845 --> 00:11:45,565
J'avais besoin de m'éclaircir les idées.
I needed to clear my head.

208
00:11:56,565 --> 00:11:58,085
Remettez-m'en un, s'il vous plaît.
I'll have another one, please.

209
00:11:58,165 --> 00:11:59,005
Tout de suite.
Coming up.

210
00:12:14,925 --> 00:12:16,725
Voilà... Maintenant on peut parler.
There... Now we can talk.

211
00:12:17,805 --> 00:12:19,405
Je m'inquiète pour toi.
I'm worried about you.

212
00:12:21,245 --> 00:12:22,525
Tu me connais, Andréa...
You know me, Andréa...

213
00:12:23,165 --> 00:12:25,085
Je suis un homme simple, j'aime ce qui est vrai.
I'm a simple guy,
I like things that feel real.

214
00:12:26,765 --> 00:12:29,485
La famille, la terre, les amis...
Family, land, friends...

215
00:12:30,045 --> 00:12:32,845
Tout ce qui se fait dans le milieu aujourd'hui est calibré, marketé...
Everything in the industry today
is calibrated, marketed...

216
00:12:33,325 --> 00:12:34,565
compliqué...
complicated...

217
00:12:35,485 --> 00:12:37,405
Alors quand on aime les choses simples,
So when you like simple things,

218
00:12:37,485 --> 00:12:38,725
il arrive un moment...
there comes a time...

219
00:12:40,605 --> 00:12:41,765
où il faut savoir partir.
when you have to walk away.

220
00:12:43,405 --> 00:12:44,405
Quitter le devant de la scène.
Step out of the limelight.

221
00:12:48,925 --> 00:12:50,685
Ça peut faire un peu peur, mais...
It can be a bit scary, but...

222
00:12:50,765 --> 00:12:52,125
ça peut aussi être beau.
it can also be beautiful.

223
00:12:55,125 --> 00:12:57,405
Dommage, j'avais un beau rôle pour toi.
It's a shame,
I had a beautiful part for you.

224
00:12:58,925 --> 00:12:59,845
Un rôle...
A part...

225
00:13:01,325 --> 00:13:02,805
La prise de la Bastille.
The storming of the Bastille.

226
00:13:03,965 --> 00:13:05,165
Entièrement filmé en clair-obscur.
Entirely shot in chiaroscuro.

227
00:13:06,965 --> 00:13:09,885
5 000 figurants derrière toi... Tu es un révolutionnaire.
5,000 extras behind you...
You're a revolutionary.

228
00:13:09,965 --> 00:13:11,445
Tu guides le peuple...
Guiding the people...

229
00:13:12,125 --> 00:13:13,085
et tu te noies dedans.
and drowning in it.

230
00:13:15,205 --> 00:13:17,125
Tout ça filmé par Xavier Beauvois.
All of this filmed by Xavier Beauvois.

231
00:13:19,805 --> 00:13:21,685
Ça sonne bien, mais je décline.
It sounds good, but I'll pass.

232
00:13:24,245 --> 00:13:26,645
D'accord. Tu préfères finir ta carrière en Père Noël ?
OK. You'd rather end your career
as Santa Claus?

233
00:13:29,165 --> 00:13:30,125
Voilà.
Right.

234
00:13:30,645 --> 00:13:31,805
-Je vais répondre. -Non.
-I'll get it.
-No.

235
00:13:38,525 --> 00:13:39,525
Je dois y aller.
I have to go.

236
00:13:40,125 --> 00:13:43,205
Je te laisse méditer sur la fin... et sa beauté.
I'll let you ponder over the end...
and its beauty.

237
00:13:50,845 --> 00:13:51,765
Un pastis.
A pastis.

238
00:13:52,445 --> 00:13:53,845
Je te promets, je ne lâcherai pas.
I promise you, I won't let up.

239
00:13:53,925 --> 00:13:55,405
Bien, continue le combat.
Good, keep up the fight.

240
00:13:55,485 --> 00:13:56,485
-À tout à l'heure. -Au revoir.
-See you later.
-Bye.

241
00:14:01,045 --> 00:14:02,045
Et Jean Reno ?
And Jean Reno?

242
00:14:02,605 --> 00:14:04,925
Je sais pas si j'ai réussi à le retourner. Je l'ai laissé mariner.
I don't know if I managed to turn him.
I left him to stew.

243
00:14:05,365 --> 00:14:07,365
J'ai pas grand espoir, mais je file à la banque.
I don't have much hope,
but I'm off to the bank.

244
00:14:07,485 --> 00:14:08,325
Ouais...
Yeah...

245
00:14:09,445 --> 00:14:10,645
Hé ! Hé ! Hé !
Hey! Hey! Hey!

246
00:14:12,325 --> 00:14:13,325
Tu vas où ?
Where are you going?

247
00:14:13,405 --> 00:14:14,805
Nulle part, juste une course à faire.
Nowhere, just an errand to run.

248
00:14:16,565 --> 00:14:18,725
Quand t'es louche comme ça, tu deviens flou.
When you're shifty like that
you get blurry.

249
00:14:18,805 --> 00:14:20,485
-Littéralement. -Ouais...
-Literally.
-Yeah...

250
00:14:20,565 --> 00:14:22,925
Bien sûr que si, Andréa ! Il est 11h et tu pues le pastis.
Of course I am, Andréa!
It's 11 am and you reek of pastis.

251
00:14:23,005 --> 00:14:24,445
Bonjour.
Hi.

252
00:14:27,125 --> 00:14:29,965
Maintenant t'es plus flou, t'es carrément pixelisé.
Well, now you're not blurry,
you're totally pixelated.

253
00:14:33,885 --> 00:14:35,165
J'ai pas compris.
I didn't get that.

254
00:14:35,245 --> 00:14:36,805
Non, laisse tomber, elle est bourrée...
No, forget it, she's drunk...

255
00:14:36,885 --> 00:14:38,245
Ah bon ?
She is?

256
00:14:38,325 --> 00:14:39,565
Rendez-vous avec un acteur en crise.
Meeting with an actor in crisis.

257
00:14:40,605 --> 00:14:43,325
Camille m'a demandé de rappliquer, alors je... Toi...
Camille asked me to rush over,
so I... You...

258
00:14:43,405 --> 00:14:44,245
Tu es...
Are you...

259
00:14:44,325 --> 00:14:46,325
Non, rien, je... juste un rendez-vous...
No, nothing, I... just a meeting...

260
00:14:46,405 --> 00:14:48,125
-OK. -Salut !
-OK.
-Bye!

261
00:14:48,205 --> 00:14:49,205
-À plus. -Ouais.
-See you.
-Yeah.

262
00:14:53,045 --> 00:14:54,125
Comment tu vas, ma chérie ?
How are you, sweetie?

263
00:14:56,565 --> 00:14:58,885
Si tu m'as fait venir à l'agence, c'est que c'est grave.
If you had me come to the agency,
it must be serious.

264
00:14:59,525 --> 00:15:00,605
Non. Grave, non...
No. Serious, no...

265
00:15:01,085 --> 00:15:03,485
-C'est juste que... -Commence pas à faire comme les autres !
-It's just that...
-Don't start acting like the rest of them!

266
00:15:03,565 --> 00:15:04,965
Me raconte pas des salades comme,
Don't give me some lie like,

267
00:15:05,045 --> 00:15:07,685
« Ozon a réécrit le rôle pour une blonde qui sait patiner. » Vas-y !
"Ozon rewrote the part for some blond
who knows how to skate." Shoot!

268
00:15:08,405 --> 00:15:09,445
Je n'ai pas eu ton contrat.
I didn't get your contract.

269
00:15:09,525 --> 00:15:11,805
La production dit qu'il y a un problème mais refuse de me dire lequel.
Production says there's an issue
but won't tell me what.

270
00:15:11,885 --> 00:15:15,005
J'ai essayé d'avoir des infos par Luchini mais il a quitté ASK, donc il répond plus.
I tried to get some info from Luchini
but he left ASK, so he's not answering.

271
00:15:17,085 --> 00:15:18,365
OK. Bon, on attend.
OK. Well, let's wait.

272
00:15:19,405 --> 00:15:20,325
On attend ?
Let's wait?

273
00:15:21,085 --> 00:15:22,605
Comment tu fais pour rester aussi zen ?
How can you stay so relaxed?

274
00:15:24,205 --> 00:15:26,805
Depuis cette histoire avec le César et Verhoeven,
Since that business
with the César and Verhoeven,

275
00:15:26,885 --> 00:15:29,405
j'essaie de pas trop... m'emballer, tu vois ?
I try not to get...
too worked up, you know?

276
00:15:29,485 --> 00:15:32,285
Tant que j'entends pas « moteur », c'est encore non.
As long as I haven't heard "camera,"
it's still a no-go.

277
00:15:33,205 --> 00:15:34,045
Impressionnant.
Impressive.

278
00:15:34,605 --> 00:15:35,885
On prend un verre ?
How about a drink?

279
00:15:35,965 --> 00:15:37,885
J'en ai bien besoin, il me faut une pause.
I could use one, I need a break.

280
00:15:37,965 --> 00:15:39,245
C'est pas à toi de me remonter le moral !
It's not for you to cheer me up!

281
00:15:40,085 --> 00:15:42,165
Faut pas tomber dans le vieux rapport agent/actrice.
Let's not fall into the old
agent/actress relationship.

282
00:15:42,245 --> 00:15:44,085
-On est au-dessus de ça, non ? -Carrément !
-We're better than that, right?
-Definitely!

283
00:15:44,565 --> 00:15:47,325
J'ai pas besoin d'une baby-sitter et ça me fait du bien de te faire du bien.
I don't need a babysitter
and it cheers me up to cheer you up.

284
00:15:48,445 --> 00:15:50,605
Attends, excuse-moi, chéri...
Hang on, excuse me, honey...

285
00:15:53,485 --> 00:15:54,485
-Tout va bien ? -Oui.
-Everything OK?
-Yes.

286
00:15:55,885 --> 00:15:56,885
Je te rejoins là-bas.
I'll meet you there.

287
00:15:57,485 --> 00:15:59,005
-OK ? -D'accord.
-OK?
-All right.

288
00:15:59,085 --> 00:16:00,285
-Oui, oui, oui. -OK.
-Yes, yes, yes.
-OK.

289
00:16:01,325 --> 00:16:02,845
-J'allais sortir. -Oui.
-I was on my way out.
-Yes.

290
00:16:03,605 --> 00:16:05,125
Écoute, non, je voulais juste...
Listen, no, I just...

291
00:16:05,205 --> 00:16:06,525
Je voulais te dire que...
I wanted to say that...

292
00:16:06,605 --> 00:16:11,645
Je l'ai pas fait exprès, mais ce matin j'ai entendu par hasard que tu parlais de ton...
I didn't mean to, but this morning
I overheard you talking about your...

293
00:16:12,285 --> 00:16:13,565
Ton projet d'agence de talent.
Your talent agency project.

294
00:16:15,405 --> 00:16:16,245
Et alors ?
And?

295
00:16:16,965 --> 00:16:18,245
C'est une excellente idée.
It's an excellent idea.

296
00:16:20,205 --> 00:16:21,125
J'aimerais t'aider.
I'd like to help.

297
00:16:23,485 --> 00:16:24,805
Papa, j'ai pas besoin de ton argent.
Dad, I don't need your money.

298
00:16:24,885 --> 00:16:26,565
Non, non, c'est pas une question d'argent.
No, no, it's not about money.

299
00:16:28,045 --> 00:16:28,885
Si...
If...

300
00:16:29,765 --> 00:16:31,245
Si tu es d'accord, j'aimerais...
If you agree, I'd like...

301
00:16:32,325 --> 00:16:33,685
J'aimerais travailler avec vous.
I'd like to work with you.

302
00:16:34,965 --> 00:16:37,045
Une petite agence familiale, sans étoiles...
A small family-run agency, no stars...

303
00:16:37,925 --> 00:16:39,565
Des talents émergents...
Emerging talents...

304
00:16:41,165 --> 00:16:42,325
J'ai vu comment vous travaillez.
I've seen how you work.

305
00:16:42,765 --> 00:16:44,165
Je ne suis pas sûr que vous puissiez changer.
I'm not sure you can change.

306
00:16:50,245 --> 00:16:51,605
Je ne peux pas revenir en arrière.
I can't turn back time.

307
00:16:52,685 --> 00:16:55,045
Je ne peux pas vous donner ce que je n'ai pas su vous donner à l'époque.
I can't give you
what I couldn't give you then.

308
00:16:58,005 --> 00:16:58,925
Mais je suis là maintenant.
But I'm here now.

309
00:17:01,365 --> 00:17:02,645
J'aimerais vous aider à démarrer.
I'd like to help you get started.

310
00:17:05,325 --> 00:17:06,245
C'est plus...
It's more...

311
00:17:06,925 --> 00:17:10,084
C'est plus concret qu'une... reconnaissance de paternité, non ?
It's more tangible than...
a recognition of paternity, right?

312
00:17:11,285 --> 00:17:12,165
C'est gentil de votre part.
It's nice of you.

313
00:17:12,805 --> 00:17:13,645
Merci.
Thanks.

314
00:17:14,285 --> 00:17:15,124
Mais, euh...
But, uh...

315
00:17:15,645 --> 00:17:17,005
Pour l'instant, je travaille pour ASK.
For the time being, I work for ASK.

316
00:17:17,685 --> 00:17:18,885
Ce n'est pas la question pour le moment.
It's irrelevant for now.

317
00:17:32,525 --> 00:17:33,605
On peut se voir demain ?
Can we meet tomorrow?

318
00:17:35,965 --> 00:17:37,165
J'ai hâte de fêter ça.
Can't wait to celebrate.

319
00:17:39,805 --> 00:17:41,125
Oui, je t'aime.
Yes, I love you.

320
00:17:42,805 --> 00:17:43,725
Je dois y aller.
Got to go.

321
00:17:44,325 --> 00:17:45,165
Fêter quoi ?
Celebrate what?

322
00:17:45,645 --> 00:17:47,045
Saigner ASK à blanc ?
Bleeding ASK dry?

323
00:17:47,125 --> 00:17:48,885
Non, pas ça. Ça n'en vaut pas la peine.
No, not that. It's not worth it.

324
00:17:48,965 --> 00:17:50,285
Pourtant, tu t'y es bien appliqué.
Still, you worked hard at it.

325
00:17:51,325 --> 00:17:52,485
Ce n'était pas difficile.
It wasn't difficult.

326
00:17:54,765 --> 00:17:56,725
J'aime quand tu essaies d'être méchant, c'est mignon.
I like it when you try to be mean,
it's cute.

327
00:17:57,485 --> 00:18:01,805
Écoute, je ne suis pas venu te regarder manger ta salade de quinoa, alors... Qu'est-ce que tu veux ?
Look, I didn't come here to watch you eat
your quinoa salad, so... What do you want?

328
00:18:05,125 --> 00:18:06,085
Il fut un temps...
There was a time...

329
00:18:06,605 --> 00:18:08,725
Il y a très longtemps, à l'âge d'or d'ASK.
A very long time ago, in ASK's golden age.

330
00:18:09,445 --> 00:18:11,965
toi et Andréa formiez le duo d'agents parfait, non ?
you and Andréa formed
the perfect agent duo, right?

331
00:18:13,565 --> 00:18:14,805
Elle était dure. Tu étais sympa.
She was tough. You were nice.

332
00:18:15,805 --> 00:18:17,085
Bonne cop, mauvaise cop.
Bad cop, good cop.

333
00:18:18,165 --> 00:18:19,885
-Une formule gagnante. -Qu'est-ce que tu veux ?
-A winning formula.
-What do you want?

334
00:18:21,645 --> 00:18:23,485
Que tu viennes chez StarMédia avec tes talents.
That you come to StarMédia
with your talents.

335
00:18:24,045 --> 00:18:26,125
On peut former une équipe, toi et moi.
We can form a team, you and I.

336
00:18:28,405 --> 00:18:30,005
Tu ne recules devant rien, n'est-ce pas ?
You stop at nothing, do you?

337
00:18:31,325 --> 00:18:32,485
Non attends, je comprends !
No wait, I get it!

338
00:18:33,685 --> 00:18:35,405
Ton rêve, c'est d'être Andréa,
Your dream is to be Andréa,

339
00:18:36,645 --> 00:18:39,405
Je sens une attirance refoulée, un conflit identitaire quelque part ?
Do I sense a repressed attraction,
an identity conflict somewhere?

340
00:18:39,485 --> 00:18:41,445
Non ? Oui ? Je ne sais pas.
No? Yes? I don't know.

341
00:18:44,525 --> 00:18:46,125
Sauf que tu ne pourras jamais être Andréa.
Except you can never be Andréa.

342
00:18:47,565 --> 00:18:50,445
Andréa est... l'exact opposé de toi.
Andréa is... the exact opposite of you.

343
00:18:51,045 --> 00:18:54,165
Non seulement elle a de la classe, mais elle n'est pas du tout lesbienne refoulée.
Not only has she got class,
but she's anything but a closet lesbian.

344
00:18:55,965 --> 00:18:57,725
Je voulais te faire une proposition.
I wanted to make you an offer.

345
00:18:57,805 --> 00:18:59,085
Tu sais où tu peux te la mettre ?
You know where you can shove it?

346
00:19:00,365 --> 00:19:01,685
Rien ne presse, Gabriel.
No rush, Gabriel.

347
00:19:02,605 --> 00:19:04,405
Je plante juste une graine dans ta tête.
I'm planting the seed in your head.

348
00:19:04,925 --> 00:19:06,125
Vois si elle germe.
Just see if it grows.

349
00:19:08,005 --> 00:19:08,845
Bonne journée.
Have a nice day.

350
00:19:15,765 --> 00:19:18,045
Je vais leur mettre la pression, ils ne sauront pas ce qui les a frappés.
I'm going to hound them down,
they won't know what hit them.

351
00:19:18,405 --> 00:19:19,765
On va s'en sortir.
We'll work it out.

352
00:19:23,365 --> 00:19:24,845
Pourquoi ? Qu'est-ce qui se passe ?
Why? What's going on?

353
00:19:24,925 --> 00:19:27,445
Il y a un problème avec Ozon. Je risque de ne pas le faire.
There's a problem with the Ozon.
I might not do it.

354
00:19:32,045 --> 00:19:33,045
Pourquoi tu souris ?
Why are you smiling?

355
00:19:34,285 --> 00:19:35,485
Je suis content de te voir.
I'm happy to see you.

356
00:19:39,605 --> 00:19:40,925
Désolé. Je suis en retard.
I'm sorry. I'm late.

357
00:19:58,165 --> 00:20:00,765
-Ozon est chez StarMédia ? -Les livraisons, c'est à l'accueil.
-Is Ozon with StarMédia?
-Deliveries are at the front desk.

358
00:20:01,525 --> 00:20:03,885
Ozon, laisse tomber, c'est l'un des meilleurs amis d'Élise.
Ozon, forget it,
he's one of Elise's best friends.

359
00:20:03,965 --> 00:20:05,325
Parce qu'elle a des amis ?
Because she has friends?

360
00:20:05,405 --> 00:20:06,245
Apparemment...
Apparently so...

361
00:20:08,845 --> 00:20:10,125
Gabriel, qu'est-ce qui se passe ?
Gabriel, what's wrong?

362
00:20:11,645 --> 00:20:12,485
Gabriel !
Gabriel!

363
00:20:14,445 --> 00:20:15,485
Tu vas me répondre ?
Will you answer me?

364
00:20:15,965 --> 00:20:16,965
On ne se parle plus ?
Are we not speaking?

365
00:20:21,965 --> 00:20:23,125
Et lui ?
And what about him?

366
00:20:24,005 --> 00:20:25,765
Il n'est plus aussi bon qu'avant.
He's not as good as he used to be.

367
00:20:25,845 --> 00:20:27,045
Oui, il a un peu vieilli.
Yes, he's aged a bit.

368
00:20:27,125 --> 00:20:29,325
Je pense que ça irait mieux à Grandjean. Bonne idée.
I think it'd be a better fit
for Grandjean. Good idea.

369
00:20:29,405 --> 00:20:31,365
D'habitude il décide vite.
He's usually quick to decide.

370
00:20:31,445 --> 00:20:34,245
S'il n'a pas appelé ce soir pour demander le script, laisse tomber.
If he hasn't called by tonight
to ask for the script, forget it.

371
00:20:34,645 --> 00:20:35,765
Tu peux ranger tes cartes.
You can pack up your cards.

372
00:20:35,845 --> 00:20:37,845
Ce projet peut sauver ASK.
This project can save ASK.

373
00:20:37,925 --> 00:20:40,845
D'abord, tu aurais dû penser à ne pas tout démolir.
First, you should have thought
about not ripping it apart.

374
00:20:40,925 --> 00:20:43,205
Mais c'est vous qui m'avez viré.
But you were the ones who fired me.

375
00:20:43,285 --> 00:20:45,125
La première grande vague de talents qui sont partis...
The first big wave of defecting talents...

376
00:20:45,845 --> 00:20:47,125
c'est ta responsabilité.
is your responsibility.

377
00:20:47,205 --> 00:20:49,805
J'ai arrêté d'être agent pour devenir producteur, Andréa, tu t'en souviens ?
I stopped being an agent
to become a producer, Andréa, remember?

378
00:20:49,885 --> 00:20:51,405
Tu n'es plus producteur !
You're not a producer anymore!

379
00:20:51,965 --> 00:20:52,965
Alors tu es quoi maintenant ?
So what are you now?

380
00:20:53,525 --> 00:20:54,725
Juste un manipulateur ?
Just a manipulator?

381
00:20:54,805 --> 00:20:56,565
C'est pas le moment de changer de disque rayé ?
Isn't it time to change the broken record?

382
00:20:57,845 --> 00:20:59,885
Ça te soulage de te défouler sur moi ?
Does it make you feel better
to take it out on me?

383
00:20:59,965 --> 00:21:02,965
Tu te sens moins coupable d'avoir laissé Élise entrer.
You feel less guilty
about letting Elise in the door.

384
00:21:03,045 --> 00:21:03,965
Exactement.
Exactly.

385
00:21:06,845 --> 00:21:07,845
C'est Arlette !
It's Arlette!

386
00:21:08,645 --> 00:21:09,485
Arlette ?
Arlette?

387
00:21:11,045 --> 00:21:11,885
Arlette ?
Arlette?

388
00:21:15,405 --> 00:21:16,885
-Qu'est-ce qui se passe ? -Ça va ?
-What's going on?
-Are you OK?

389
00:21:19,565 --> 00:21:22,885
Je ne suis ni vétérinaire ni spécialiste des chiens, mais il est glacé.
I'm not a vet or a dog expert,
but he's ice cold.

390
00:21:28,525 --> 00:21:30,365
Je suis désolé, Arlette. Il est parti.
I'm sorry, Arlette. He's gone.

391
00:21:31,165 --> 00:21:32,205
Toutes mes condoléances.
My condolences.

392
00:22:10,325 --> 00:22:11,805
Il sera là dans 5 minutes.
He'll be here in 5 minutes.

393
00:22:28,245 --> 00:22:30,085
Gardez à l'esprit qu'il est mort dans son sommeil.
Keep in mind that he died in his sleep.

394
00:22:31,445 --> 00:22:33,245
C'est la meilleure façon de mourir pour un chien.
It's the best way to die for a dog.

395
00:22:34,285 --> 00:22:35,645
Et pour n'importe qui, d'ailleurs.
And for anyone, in fact.

396
00:22:38,285 --> 00:22:41,605
J'ai réservé une place pour lui au cimetière pour chiens d'Asnières.
I reserved a plot for him
at the dog cemetery in Asnières.

397
00:22:42,645 --> 00:22:44,645
Je les préviens, ils viendront le chercher.
I'll let them know,
they'll come pick him up.

398
00:22:46,405 --> 00:22:48,205
S'il y a quoi que ce soit que je puisse faire pour vous...
If there's anything I can do for you...

399
00:22:49,725 --> 00:22:51,405
Pouvez-vous nous laisser, s'il vous plaît ?
Can you leave us, please?

400
00:22:52,085 --> 00:22:53,245
Bien sûr.
Of course.

401
00:23:04,405 --> 00:23:07,765
C'est avec le service juridique, je le récupère cet après-midi.
It's with the legal department
so I'll get it back this afternoon.

402
00:23:08,365 --> 00:23:09,285
Je vous tiens au courant.
I'll let you know.

403
00:23:10,445 --> 00:23:11,805
-D'accord. -Élise.
-OK.
-Elise.

404
00:23:14,485 --> 00:23:15,405
Je peux te parler ?
Can I talk to you?

405
00:23:15,885 --> 00:23:16,725
Je dois y aller.
I have to go.

406
00:23:16,805 --> 00:23:18,005
Sans tes gardes du corps.
Without your guard dogs.

407
00:23:19,205 --> 00:23:20,685
Les filles ? Merci.
Girls? Thanks.

408
00:23:22,725 --> 00:23:23,685
Qu'est-ce qu'il y a ?
What's up?

409
00:23:24,645 --> 00:23:25,485
Sofia...
Sofia...

410
00:23:26,245 --> 00:23:27,405
C'était toi ?
Was that you?

411
00:23:27,485 --> 00:23:29,485
Je ne vois pas de quoi tu parles.
I don't know what you're talking about.

412
00:23:30,645 --> 00:23:32,085
Tu vas me frapper ?
Are you going to hit me?

413
00:23:33,245 --> 00:23:34,365
Non. Et puis...
No. Besides...

414
00:23:35,405 --> 00:23:37,845
Je ne vais pas te donner plus de munitions pour me faire pression.
I'm not going to give you
any more ammunition to pressure me.

415
00:23:37,925 --> 00:23:40,045
C'est toi qui te mets cette pression.
You put that pressure on yourself.

416
00:23:40,765 --> 00:23:42,965
On dirait que tu tiens à ta petite Sofia !
Looks like you care
about your little Sofia!

417
00:23:43,045 --> 00:23:43,965
Merde.
Shit.

418
00:23:45,405 --> 00:23:47,525
Un rôle face à Luchini dans le film d'Ozon...
A part opposite Luchini in Ozon's film...

419
00:23:48,125 --> 00:23:49,645
Ça ne se reproduira pas de sitôt.
That won't happen again any time soon.

420
00:23:50,885 --> 00:23:53,565
Accepter un poste d'agent, c'est vraiment un tel sacrifice ?
Is accepting a job as an agent
such a sacrifice?

421
00:23:53,645 --> 00:23:54,525
Avec toi, oui.
With you, yes.

422
00:23:56,085 --> 00:23:57,125
Ça ne va pas te tuer.
It's not going to kill you.

423
00:23:58,045 --> 00:23:59,365
C'est très formateur.
It's very formative.

424
00:24:00,285 --> 00:24:02,765
Et puis, tu n'en as pas assez de tout ramener à toi ?
Besides, aren't you tired
of making everything so personal?

425
00:24:03,125 --> 00:24:05,205
Arrête de faire l'enfant gâté : grandis !
Stop acting like a spoiled brat: grow up!

426
00:24:05,285 --> 00:24:06,125
Écoute...
Listen...

427
00:24:06,605 --> 00:24:07,845
Mes clients ne me quitteront pas.
My clients won't leave me.

428
00:24:07,925 --> 00:24:09,445
Même si ASK coule...
Even if ASK goes under...

429
00:24:09,965 --> 00:24:12,485
Je peux ouvrir mon agence... quand je veux. Je n'ai pas besoin de toi.
I can open my agency... anytime.
I don't need you.

430
00:24:12,565 --> 00:24:13,925
Oui, je crois que tu as raison.
Yes, I think you're right.

431
00:24:15,325 --> 00:24:17,085
Mais pense à ce que dira ta chérie
But think about
what your sweetheart will say

432
00:24:17,165 --> 00:24:20,365
quand elle apprendra que tu l'as sacrifiée pour tes ambitions personnelles.
when she learns you sacrificed her
for your personal ambitions.

433
00:24:21,445 --> 00:24:22,685
Elle comprendra.
She'll understand.

434
00:24:22,845 --> 00:24:24,685
Après ce que tu lui as fait sur le film de Julien Doré ?
After what you did to her
on Julien Doré's film?

435
00:24:26,565 --> 00:24:27,645
Tu ne connais vraiment pas les femmes.
You really don't know women.

436
00:24:28,885 --> 00:24:32,285
Tu devrais me remercier. Je te donne une chance de te racheter.
You should be thanking me.
I'm giving you a chance to make up for it.

437
00:24:32,805 --> 00:24:33,805
Tu me tiendras au courant ?
You'll let me know?

438
00:24:41,805 --> 00:24:42,765
Jean Reno arrive !
Jean Reno is on his way!

439
00:24:42,845 --> 00:24:45,485
Les enjeux sont importants, alors tout le monde s'y remet, OK ?
There's a lot at stake,
so everyone gets back to work, OK?

440
00:24:45,565 --> 00:24:47,445
On est dans une agence qui bouge, alors on va tout déchirer !
We're in a buzzing agency,
let's knock 'em dead!

441
00:24:48,165 --> 00:24:49,725
Je veux dire... On assure.
I mean... We're on fire.

442
00:24:49,805 --> 00:24:51,725
Donc... c'est comme être figurant :
So... it's like being an extra:

443
00:24:51,805 --> 00:24:54,525
sortez vos portables et commencez à appeler sans arrêt,
pull out your cell phones
and start calling nonstop,

444
00:24:54,605 --> 00:24:57,285
appelez l'accueil, les fixes, tous les postes...
call the front desk,
the landlines, every desk...

445
00:24:57,365 --> 00:24:58,485
Faites sonner les téléphones.
Let's keep it ringing.

446
00:24:58,565 --> 00:25:00,405
Cette agence n'est pas à l'agonie !
This agency is not on its deathbed!

447
00:25:00,485 --> 00:25:02,445
Je veux dire... elle n'est pas en difficulté...
I mean... it's not in trouble...

448
00:25:02,525 --> 00:25:05,205
On est débordés... On croule sous les projets !
We're drowning under...
We're swamped with projects!

449
00:25:05,285 --> 00:25:06,125
Allez ! On y va !
All right! Go!

450
00:25:06,205 --> 00:25:07,125
Allez !
Go!

451
00:25:07,725 --> 00:25:09,085
Hervé, Camille.
Hervé, Camille.

452
00:25:09,165 --> 00:25:10,205
OK, j'ai besoin de vous.
OK, I need you.

453
00:25:10,285 --> 00:25:11,765
Vous allez m'apporter une version du scénario
You'll hand me a version of the script

454
00:25:11,845 --> 00:25:13,845
couverte de remarques dithyrambiques sur Jean Reno.
scribbled with raving remarks
about Jean Reno.

455
00:25:13,925 --> 00:25:15,605
Comme si Xavier Beauvois l'avait écrit.
As if Xavier Beauvois had written it.

456
00:25:15,685 --> 00:25:16,805
Allez, on y va !
All right, go!

457
00:25:22,045 --> 00:25:23,965
-Jean ! Comment tu vas ? -Bien !
-Jean! How are you?
-I'm fine!

458
00:25:24,045 --> 00:25:24,965
Bien.
Good.

459
00:25:27,445 --> 00:25:29,485
Un instant, s'il vous plaît. ASK, que puis-je faire pour vous ?
One moment, please. ASK, may I help you?

460
00:25:31,805 --> 00:25:32,925
Qu'est-ce qui se passe ici ?
What's going on here?

461
00:25:34,125 --> 00:25:34,965
C'est lundi.
It's Monday.

462
00:25:35,805 --> 00:25:37,165
-Oui, apportez-le-moi. -Venez.
-Yes, bring it to me.
-Come.

463
00:25:37,245 --> 00:25:38,285
C'est lundi.
It's Monday.

464
00:25:41,525 --> 00:25:42,365
Jean...
Jean...

465
00:25:42,445 --> 00:25:43,325
Arlette ?
Arlette?

466
00:25:44,605 --> 00:25:45,445
Oui.
Yes.

467
00:25:46,205 --> 00:25:47,125
Arlette !
Arlette!

468
00:25:50,045 --> 00:25:51,565
Ça fait une éternité.
It's been ages.

469
00:25:55,365 --> 00:25:56,205
Vous allez bien ?
Are you OK?

470
00:25:57,285 --> 00:25:58,285
Jean Gabin est mort.
Jean Gabin is dead.

471
00:25:58,365 --> 00:26:01,245
Jean Gabin, oui ! Il est...
Jean Gabin, yes! He's...

472
00:26:03,285 --> 00:26:04,125
Oui.
Yes.

473
00:26:04,765 --> 00:26:05,925
Il va tellement me manquer.
I'll miss him so much.

474
00:26:06,725 --> 00:26:08,005
Il nous manque à tous...
We all miss him...

475
00:26:08,685 --> 00:26:10,445
Il était d'une intelligence exceptionnelle.
He was exceptionally smart.

476
00:26:11,165 --> 00:26:12,045
Oui.
Yes.

477
00:26:13,325 --> 00:26:14,565
Et il aimait les choses simples...
And he enjoyed simple things...

478
00:26:14,645 --> 00:26:16,445
Oui... Manger...
Yes... Eating...

479
00:26:17,645 --> 00:26:19,365
-Se promener... -Dormir...
-Taking a walk...
-Sleeping...

480
00:26:19,445 --> 00:26:20,725
Courir après un ballon...
Running after a ball...

481
00:26:21,485 --> 00:26:22,725
Ça, je ne savais pas.
That, I didn't know.

482
00:26:22,805 --> 00:26:24,125
Oui, bon, dans sa jeunesse.
Yes, well, in his youth.

483
00:26:26,805 --> 00:26:27,645
Mais ces derniers temps...
But lately...

484
00:26:29,285 --> 00:26:30,485
il était rarement d'humeur.
he was rarely up for it.

485
00:26:34,525 --> 00:26:35,365
Bon.
Well.

486
00:26:36,125 --> 00:26:36,965
Je dois y aller.
I have to go.

487
00:26:37,845 --> 00:26:38,885
Merci pour votre soutien.
Thank you for your support.

488
00:26:38,965 --> 00:26:40,285
De rien, Arlette.
You're welcome, Arlette.

489
00:26:46,565 --> 00:26:47,645
Qu'est-ce qu'il y a ?
What is it?

490
00:26:48,405 --> 00:26:49,965
-Alzheimer ? -Non.
-Alzheimer's?
-No.

491
00:26:50,845 --> 00:26:51,725
C'est le deuil.
It's grief.

492
00:26:53,285 --> 00:26:56,445
-C'est Noémie qui a pensé à vous. -Oui.
-Noémie is the one who thought of you.
-Yes.

493
00:26:56,525 --> 00:26:59,925
En lisant le scénario, j'ai imaginé Jean Reno ! C'était...
When I read the script,
I pictured Jean Reno! It was...

494
00:27:00,005 --> 00:27:02,165
-une évidence. -Merci.
-obvious.
-Thank you.

495
00:27:02,885 --> 00:27:06,085
Bien... Alors Jean, il faut nous dire franchement.
Right... Now, Jean,
you have to tell us straight up.

496
00:27:06,165 --> 00:27:07,685
Vous voulez le faire ou pas ?
Do you want to do it or not?

497
00:27:07,765 --> 00:27:09,245
Vous aviez raison, Andréa.
You were right, Andréa.

498
00:27:09,325 --> 00:27:11,965
Je ne veux pas que mon dernier rôle soit le Père Noël.
I don't want my last part
to be Santa Claus.

499
00:27:12,045 --> 00:27:13,605
J'aimerais lire le scénario.
I'd like to read the script.

500
00:27:16,085 --> 00:27:17,365
Ça vient d'arriver de chez Beauvois !
This just came in from Beauvois!

501
00:27:21,165 --> 00:27:24,285
Xavier voulait faire quelques ajustements au cas où ce serait vous.
Xavier wanted to make a few adjustments
in case it'd be you.

502
00:27:24,365 --> 00:27:26,685
Voilà. C'est donc la dernière version.
There. So this is the latest version.

503
00:27:26,765 --> 00:27:27,965
Tout frais sorti du four.
Fresh out of the oven.

504
00:27:35,125 --> 00:27:37,645
Les gens de ce métier n'arrêtent pas de me surprendre.
People in this business
never cease to surprise me.

505
00:27:38,405 --> 00:27:39,485
Oh là là ! Waouh !
Oh my! Wow!

506
00:27:41,605 --> 00:27:42,965
Sentez cet amour !
Feel the love!

507
00:27:48,045 --> 00:27:48,885
Ouais, salut...
Yeah, hi...

508
00:27:50,445 --> 00:27:51,325
Comment tu vas ?
How are you?

509
00:27:52,085 --> 00:27:53,325
Elle me manque déjà.
I miss her already.

510
00:27:53,405 --> 00:27:56,565
Quand elle est avec toi elle est pénible, mais quand elle part elle te manque.
When she's with you she's a bother,
but when she's gone you miss her.

511
00:27:57,165 --> 00:27:58,165
Bon sang, Colette !
Damn it, Colette!

512
00:27:58,245 --> 00:28:00,125
Écoute, j'ai déjà merdé avec l'agence,
Look, I already messed up with the agency,

513
00:28:00,205 --> 00:28:03,405
alors si tu me dis que je suis une mauvaise mère, je crois que je vais craquer.
so if you tell me I'm a lousy mother,
I don't think I can keep it together.

514
00:28:04,405 --> 00:28:05,405
Je suis désolée.
I'm sorry.

515
00:28:05,485 --> 00:28:07,005
Je n'ai jamais dit que tu étais une mauvaise mère.
I never said you were a lousy mother.

516
00:28:07,605 --> 00:28:09,685
Mais tu sais, elle ne l'a jamais fait avec moi...
But you know, she never did it with me...

517
00:28:10,125 --> 00:28:11,125
Les pleurs pour évacuer le stress.
The stress-release crying.

518
00:28:11,845 --> 00:28:13,525
Hé ! C'est bon. Peut-être qu'elle ne le fera jamais.
Hey! It's all right. Maybe she never will.

519
00:28:13,605 --> 00:28:15,205
Ça ne veut pas dire qu'elle n'est pas heureuse avec toi.
It doesn't mean she's not happy with you.

520
00:28:17,485 --> 00:28:19,085
Dis donc... J'ai vraiment envie de la voir.
Man... I really want to see her.

521
00:28:20,685 --> 00:28:23,405
Quand tu veux. Je veux dire... Quand tu peux.
Well anytime you want.
I mean... Anytime you can.

522
00:28:23,925 --> 00:28:24,765
Ouais...
Yeah...

523
00:28:25,765 --> 00:28:26,925
Je te tiens au courant, OK ?
I'll let you know, OK?

524
00:28:28,445 --> 00:28:30,365
OK. Alright, bonne nuit, au revoir.
OK. All right, good night, bye.

525
00:28:39,725 --> 00:28:41,085
Fermeture des portes.
Doors closing.

526
00:28:56,565 --> 00:28:58,085
Bonjour, Madame la Productrice...
Hello, Mrs. Producer...

527
00:28:58,885 --> 00:29:00,205
Tu m'as fait peur.
You scared me.

528
00:29:01,845 --> 00:29:02,685
Des croissants.
Croissants.

529
00:29:04,405 --> 00:29:05,485
Oh, merveilleux.
Oh, marvelous.

530
00:29:08,205 --> 00:29:09,445
Longue nuit ?
Long night?

531
00:29:10,485 --> 00:29:11,725
Putain, oui.
Damn it, yeah.

532
00:29:13,965 --> 00:29:17,325
J'ai étudié le projet sous tous les angles...
I studied the project from all angles...

533
00:29:18,805 --> 00:29:20,685
Revu tout le budget...
Went over the whole budget again...

534
00:29:21,645 --> 00:29:24,405
Le tournage au Luxembourg, les crédits d'impôt...
Shooting in Luxemburg, tax credits...

535
00:29:24,485 --> 00:29:26,605
